       POSIX.1  specifies  that nniiccee() should return the new nice value.  How‐
       ever, the raw Linux system call returns 0 on  success.   Likewise,  the
       nniiccee()  wrapper  function provided in glibc 2.2.3 and earlier returns 0
       on success.

       Since glibc 2.2.4, the nniiccee() wrapper function provided by  glibc  pro‐
       vides  conformance  to  POSIX.1 by calling ggeettpprriioorriittyy(2) to obtain the
       new nice value, which is then returned to the caller.

